{
  "id": "dsa-021",
  "title": "Program to Print Floyd's Triangle - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Given an integer </span><b><strong>n</strong></b><span>, print </span><b><strong>Floyd's Triangle</strong></b><span> with </span><b><strong>n </strong></b><span>rows. Floyd's Triangle is a right-angled triangular pattern formed using consecutive natural numbers starting from 1.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example</strong></b><span>:</span></p><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Input</strong></b><span>: 6</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output</strong></b><span>:</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"420851452\" height=\"236\" src=\"/images/dsa-021-img-1.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260310123037263136/420851452.webp 233w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260310123037263136/420851452-100.webp 99w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260310123037263136/420851452-200.webp 197w\" width=\"233\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure></blockquote></div><a id=\"practiceBanner\" class=\"ArticlePracticeBanner_practiceDivBanner__idAxy ArticlePracticeBanner_desktopOnly__r87aW rc0\" href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/floyds-triangle1222/1\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"display:block\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><div class=\"ArticlePracticeBanner_recommendedDiv__7Q5go\">Try It Yourself<div class=\"ArticlePracticeBanner_icon__UeNv9\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/dsa-021-img-2.svg\" alt=\"redirect icon\" class=\"ArticlePracticeBanner_redirectIcon__mJJ_m undefined\"></div></div></a><div class=\"html-chunk\"><h3 id=\"using-nested-loops-on-time-and-o1-space\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Using Nested Loops - O(n²) Time and O(1) Space</span></h3><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The pattern can be printed using two nested loops. The outer loop controls the number of rows, while the inner loop prints the numbers in each row. A variable val is used to keep track of the current number, which is incremented after each print so that the numbers appear in increasing order across the triangle.</span></p></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><br><b><strong>Step-wise Approach:&nbsp;</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Initialize a variable val = 1 to store the current number to print.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Run an outer loop from 1 to n to iterate through the rows.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>For each row i, run an inner loop from 1 to i.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Print the current value of val.</span></li><li value=\"5\"><span>Increment val after printing each number.</span></li><li value=\"6\"><span>After completing each row, move to the next line.</span></li></ul><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">C++</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"cpp\" data-main-code-start=\"3\" data-main-code-end=\"12\">\n    <code class=\"language-cpp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span class=\"driver-code\"><span></span><span class=\"c1\">//Driver Code Starts</span>\n<span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">std</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">//Driver Code Ends</span>\n</span>\n<span class=\"main-code\"><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">printfloydtriangle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">cout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">cout</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">endl</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</span>\n<span class=\"driver-code\"><span class=\"c1\">//Driver Code Starts</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printfloydtriangle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">//Driver Code Ends</span>\n</span></pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">Java</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"java\" data-main-code-start=\"3\" data-main-code-end=\"11\">\n    <code class=\"language-java\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span class=\"driver-code\"><span></span><span class=\"c1\">//Driver Code Starts</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">GFG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">//Driver Code Ends</span>\n</span>\n<span class=\"main-code\"><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">static</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">printfloydtriangle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span 